# src/apps/daemon/internal/networking/covert

## Purpose
Implements covert or obfuscated networking helpers retained as part of the daemon transport surface.

## Contents
Contains Go transport/protocol code and supporting models used to establish or carry traffic through covert networking modes.

## Interfaces and dependencies
Consumed by higher networking/routing orchestration and depends on lower-level sockets, protocols, configuration, and cancellation facilities.

## Invariants
Network operations are bounded and cancellable, malformed peer/input data is rejected safely, connection resources are closed on failure, and transport-specific details do not leak into unrelated orchestration layers.